  A39 walk test books line by line (test/banking/bank-inbox-day.test.mjs).

  What it is: every party, IBAN, reference and amount is invented for this test. The account IBAN is the
  published PostFinance sample (CH93 0076 2011 6238 5295 7); the other IBANs are invented numbers with a
  correct check pair. It is hand-built to the SIX Swiss Payment Standards camt.053 shape (Stmt with
  ElctrncSeqNb, OPBD and CLBD, BOOK entries, TxDtls with Refs, RltdPties and RmtInf).

  Four values come from the books the test builds, so they are placeholders the test fills in before the
  import: the QR reference of the invoice TILL issued (QRR_INVOICE), and the PmtInfId and the two
  EndToEndIds TILL wrote into its own pain.001 run (PMTINF, E2E_1, E2E_2), each spelled between two
  pairs of at-signs below.

  The lines (all booked 2026-09-30, CHF):
    +1081.00  a QR credit for the issued invoice (QRR reference)
     +500.00  a credit without reference, already on the books from the migration
      -12.00  the bank's account fee
     -108.10  a card purchase with Vorsteuer
    -1000.00  TILL's payment run, booked one detail per payment (600.00 and 400.00), both details
              carrying the booking's own AcctSvcrRef (the shared-ref deviation L7 (a) keeps apart)
    -5000.00  a transfer to the own savings account
  Opening 20000.00, closing 15460.90: the closing balance is the opening plus every line.

  (Elements are named in prose without angle brackets on purpose: the regex parser scans the whole
  payload, so a tag token inside this comment would be read as a real element.)
-->
